body:
GA,

Marcus identified during live test review that Kai cannot type fractions or square roots as answers.
Current grader uses parseFloat() which fails silently on "4/3" (parses as 4) and "sqrt(5)" (NaN).
This is blocking accurate self-testing. Implement the following in exam.html.

TASK 1 — parseStudentAnswer(str) function

Replace all uses of parseFloat(el.value) in gradeExam() with parseStudentAnswer(el.value).

The function must handle:
  "4"       -> 4
  "-8"      -> -8
  "1.5"     -> 1.5
  "4/3"     -> 1.33333...
  "-3/4"    -> -0.75
  "sqrt(5)" -> 2.2360...
  "sqrt5"   -> 2.2360... (no parens also valid)
  "2sqrt(3)" -> 3.4641...
  "-sqrt(2)" -> -1.4142...
  "2/3"     -> 0.6666...

Implementation sketch:
  function parseStudentAnswer(str) {
      if (!str) return NaN;
      str = str.trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, '');
      // Fraction
      var frac = str.match(/^(-?\d+)\/(\d+)$/);
      if (frac) return parseInt(frac[1]) / parseInt(frac[2]);
      // Sqrt with optional coefficient: e.g. 2sqrt(3) or -sqrt(5)
      var sq = str.match(/^(-?\d*(?:\.\d+)?)sqrt\(?(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)\)?$/);
      if (sq) {
          var c = sq[1] === '' ? 1 : sq[1] === '-' ? -1 : parseFloat(sq[1]);
          return c * Math.sqrt(parseFloat(sq[2]));
      }
      return parseFloat(str);
  }

TASK 2 — Format guide banner

Add immediately after the examSubtitle paragraph (id="examSubtitle"), before the progress strip:

  <div class="answer-format-guide" id="answerFormatGuide">
    <strong>Answer formats:</strong> whole numbers (5 or -8) &nbsp;·&nbsp; fractions (4/3) &nbsp;·&nbsp; square roots (sqrt(5) or 2sqrt(3))
  </div>

CSS in exam.html style block:
  .answer-format-guide {
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      background: var(--bg-card);
      border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 8px 14px;
      margin: 8px 0 16px;
      line-height: 1.5;
  }

TASK 3 — Tighten tolerance

In gradeExam(), the default tolerance is currently 0.1. Change default to 0.01:
  tolerance: inp.tolerance || 0.01

(Some questions have explicit tolerance set — do not change those, only the fallback default.)

TASK 4 — Check answer format hints in feedback

For number inputs that are graded wrong, the feedback_wrong message should hint at the correct
format. If q.inputs has a number input and the answer is not an integer, append to feedback_wrong:
"(Accepted: whole numbers, fractions like 4/3, square roots like sqrt(5))"
Only append this if the answer is not an integer (answer % 1 !== 0).

SCOPE
Only exam.html changes. Do not touch data files — GR will update stored answers separately.

DEFINITION OF DONE
1. Kai can type "4/3" in any number input and it grades correctly against 1.333 answer (tolerance 0.01)
2. Kai can type "sqrt(5)" and it grades correctly against 2.236 answer
3. Format guide is visible on every exam page below the subtitle, before the first question
4. Default tolerance is 0.01

Coaching protocol: after completing, send me (1) what you built, (2) what you learned, (3) what you'd do differently.

— FA
